    "title": "Duke uses big second half to pull away from TCU, advance to Sweet 16",
    "text": "For the second straight game, Duke’s opponent came out and gave the Blue Devils its best shot to start the second half, as TCU quickly turned a four-point halftime deficit into a two-point lead.That was when Cameron Boozer and the Blue Devils said enough, going on a 28-10 run to pull away from the Horned Frogs in a 81-58 win to advance to the Sweet 16.AdvertisementWhile the Boozer brothers were quiet in the first half, combining for four points, it was Isaiah Evans and Maliq Brown who picked up the slack, combining for 25 points as Jon Scheyer’s squad took a 38-34 advantage into the break.The Horned Frog responded, but it wasn’t enough as Cameron and Cayden Boozer scored back-to-back baskets while getting fouled before Nikolas Khamenia hit a three to give the Blue Devils a nine-point edge with 11:48 to go.Cameron Boozer, whose only points in the first half came at the free-throw line, started showing why he was the ACC Player of the Year and likely Wooden Award winner, scoring 17 points in the final 20 minutes, on his way to another double-double 19 points and 11 rebounds. He was joined by Evans, who put up 17 points, while Maliq Brown (12) and Dame Sarr (14) all finished in double-digits.Patrick Ngongba returned to the floor for the first time since the NC State game, scoring four points with four rebounds and four assists in 13 minutes.AdvertisementThe No. 1 seed Blue Devils now face the winner of Kansas/St. John’s in Washington, DC, in the Sweet 16 on Friday, March 27.Bue Devils in controlDuke has controlled most of the second half and hold a 22-point advantage at the last media timeout.2:54 2H - Duke 74, TCU 52Dame Sarr breaks it openHe nails a three-pointer from the corner and Duke is in control with 8:25 to go.8:25 2ND - Duke 64, TCU 50Jamie Dixon gets a technicalCayden Boozer hits both free throws. Duke up 61-50.Khamenia from three!Duke on a 9-0 run after a three-pointer from Nikolas Khamenia, and TCU takes a timeout.11:48 2ND - Duke 53, TCU 44Boozer brothers stepping upCayden and Cameron just went back-to-back with and-ones to give Duke a six-point lead.Advertisement13:09 2ND - Duke 50, TCU 44Duke continues to be sloppyTwo straight turnovers and TCU ties the game. Isaiah Evans, as per usual today, comes up big with a basket and a foul.14:27 2H - Duke 44, TCU 42Cameron Boozer breaks droughtThe freshman scores his first basket of the game to stop a long scoring drought by the Blue Devils. He then gets a steal and gets fouled while shooting.15:26 2ND - Duke 40, TCU 40TCU goes on 6-0 lead to start second halfThe Blue Devils look all out of sync, turning the ball over and have gone flat from the floor. Jon Scheyer takes a timeout.16:11 2H - TCU 40, Duke 38Duke struggling from the floorThe Blue Devils haven't scored a field goal in more than seven minutes. The Horned Frogs have tied the game at 38 with 16:23 to go.AdvertisementHALFTIME: Duke 38, TCU 34Duke holding four-point leadThe Blue Devils are up four with the ball and 30 seconds left before halftime.0:30 1H - Duke 38, TCU 34Cameron Boozer gets called for flagrantHe elbowed a TCU defender while driving to the basket.All Duke and Isaiah Evans right nowThe guard has 13 points and the Blue Devils have built an eight-point lead, forcing Jamie Dixon to take a timeout.5:24 1ST - Duke 31, TCU 23Evans leading the way for DukeIsaiah Evans is up to 11 points for the Blue Devils, while Cameron and Cayden Boozer have combined for four points.Devils up by five at 7:34 timeout.Advertisement7:34 1H - Duke 27, TCU 22Back and forth affairBoth teams have settled in and are going back and forth. Nikolas Khamenia will go to the line after the timeout with the Blue Devils down one.11:51 1ST - TCU 15, Duke 14Ngongba's impact feltThe center scores a basket to put Duke up 9-7.Duke, TCU trading baskets earlyBoth teams have came out trying to feel each other out early on.16:00 1H - Duke 7, TCU 7Patrick Ngongba makes his first appearanceThe Duke center checked in for the first time in the game and is currently on the floor. Big news to watch is how many minutes he plays.Same five starters for DukeThe Blue Devils will start with Cayden Boozer, Isaiah Evans, Dame Sarr, Maliq Brown and Cameron Boozer on the floor against TCU.Patrick Ngongba on the floor warming upThe center is expected to play for the first time since the NC State game after dealing with a foot injury, but on limited minutes.AdvertisementHotel sendoff for the Blue DevilsThis article originally appeared on Duke Wire: Duke uses big second half to pull away from TCU, advance to Sweet 16",
